{"name":"Lisbon","slug":"lisbon","region":"Europe","lat":38.72,"lon":-9.14,"seasons":{"DJF":{"season_name":"Dec 2026–Feb 2027","years":[1951,1952,1953,1954,1955,1956,1957,1958,1959,1960,1961,1962,1963,1964,1965,1966,1967,1968,1969,1970,1971,1972,1973,1974,1975,1976,1977,1978,1979,1980,1981,1982,1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989,1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"roni_lead":[-0.38,0.98,0.04,0.84,-0.31,-1.31,-0.14,1.16,0.24,0.04,0.08,-0.16,-0.3,1.06,-0.64,1.86,-0.03,-0.08,0.56,0.67,-0.57,-0.4,1.82,-1.63,-0.45,-0.95,1.04,0.89,-0.08,0.52,-0.06,-0.17,2.03,-0.9,-0.61,-0.18,1.0,1.2,-1.71,-0.23,0.27,1.2,0.1,0.46,0.97,-0.93,-0.25,2.22,-1.33,-1.06,-0.55,-0.18,1.18,0.17,0.7,-0.18,0.73,-1.33,-0.38,0.86,-1.61,-0.91,0.21,-0.22,0.35,2.03,-0.96,-0.82,0.62,0.15,-1.37,-1.08,-1.1,1.3,-0.76],"paragraph":"Dec–Feb in Lisbon has warmed by about 0.15 °C per decade since 1951, roughly 1.1 °C in all. There is a suggestive but uncertain El Niño signal on temperature: after El Niño conditions in the preceding fall, Dec–Feb tends to run warmer. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 40% of a normal year-to-year swing, a noticeable tilt, though ordinary variability can easily outweigh it, roughly as much warmth as 18 years of the long-term trend. Dec–Feb rainfall has fallen by about 5% per decade, with no clear El Niño link. Humidity shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a more humid Dec–Feb, and this year's shift is substantial. For Dec 2026–Feb 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is likely (about 75% chance), about 0.8 °C above the 1991–2020 average, mostly because of the long-term warming trend rather than El Niño; a more humid season than normal is likely (about 65% chance). The El Niño expected for Sep–Nov 2026 is stronger than any in the record used here, so the outlook extends the historical relationship beyond what has been observed. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":12.1175,"trend_per_decade":0.1499,"trend_p":0.0001,"trend_total_since_1951":1.1241,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.148,"enso_p":0.092,"confidence":"Suggestive","survives_fdr":false,"fraction_explained":0.0389,"intrinsic_sd":0.6893,"effect_this_season":0.2738,"effect_ratio":0.3972,"size":"Noticeable","size_typical_el_nino":"Negligible","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":null,"expected_anomaly_2027":0.7665,"forecast_mean":12.8841,"forecast_sd":0.7371,"p_below":0.0856,"p_near":0.1434,"p_above":0.771,"forecast_words":"Likely (77%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":false,"enso_effect_shrunk_per_degC":0.1082,"shrink_factor":0.7312,"effect_this_season_raw":0.3744,"trend_part_2027":0.4927,"roni_upper_within_record":false,"years_of_warming_equivalent":18.2669,"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.1757,"trend_p":0.0032,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.0733,"enso_p":0.6477,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shift_this_season":0.1853,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.158,"trend_p":0.0001,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.1597,"enso_p":0.1495,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shift_this_season":0.404,"lines_cross":false},"p95":{"trend_per_decade":0.14,"trend_p":0.0033,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.1319,"enso_p":0.3267,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shift_this_season":0.3337,"lines_cross":false},"tails":{"enso_difference":0.0586,"enso_difference_p":0.7521,"trend_difference":-0.0356,"trend_difference_p":0.589}},"values":[11.423,11.266,11.471,11.145,12.651,11.463,10.625,11.577,12.349,12.093,11.825,12.218,11.445,11.658,10.527,13.324,11.238,11.415,11.931,11.766,10.843,11.219,11.371,11.701,12.016,10.885,12.171,13.219,13.093,12.309,11.197,12.931,11.167,12.098,12.193,12.117,11.911,12.734,11.853,13.274,11.097,11.197,12.109,11.843,13.106,